  "body": "**Status: scoped negative result; no new \u03ba.** This contribution exhausts the same-invocation three-role cycle subdomain on the selected PR1094 T16 owner map. It finds no capacity-feasible cycle that strictly lowers the selected complex moment.\n\n## Assignment and pins\n\n- Track/card: `incumbent-optimization` / `selected-packing`\n- Accepted OS seed: `c37585e64a1b0aaf41a29afcbfd3f5c7`\n- Priority revision: 3; exact base: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`\n- Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`\n- Selected owner source: `research/complex-t16-rare-pattern-exchanges/data/PLAN.json` SHA-256 `7bd786ba8e66408f02aa9ef446eaf20c1bfe981ea2e4dd1e5a929f0aa7767bc0`; `OWNERS.json.gz` SHA-256 `87902c528dfab7d503dcf8a784260e3ab6fb7424c418a1820f7261f25be7b6bc`\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe exact compressed census covers all 144 calls and 480 roles per call:\n\n- 49,408 ordered supported `(idle slack, width)` type patterns\n- 4,417 capacity-feasible patterns\n- 255 distinct ordered transfer states\n- 35 distinct old/new idle-rank histogram transitions\n- 19 exact histogram ties; 16 strictly higher-cost transitions; 0 lower-cost transitions\n\nBoth selected rational moment engines price all distinct transitions at the accepted complex endpoint. The minimum strict increase is certified by the Mercator interval in `RESULT.json` and independently by the base-two interval; the package also includes a source witness. A separate improving arithmetic fixture validates the sign convention. The selected bit supplier is repriced with its existing surcharge and remains unchanged; the complex side still binds. The fixed-word cap remains `a < 1690054109089/10^15`, hence `\u03ba < 1690054109089/1001690054109089`; this domain realizes 0% of its packing headroom.\n\n## Scope and overlap\n\nThis is a scoped census of same-call permutations among three distinct occupied groups, not a global owner-packing optimum. Cross-call cycles, paths into free groups, longer sequences and changed local words are excluded.\n\nPR #1790 covers the selected PR1094 map's two-role swaps and leaves three-role cycles open. PR #1154 has a positive three-owner cycle on the different PR1117 route and changed local word; it does not census this selected map. PR #1617 and #1819 cover adjacent neutral-relocation classes.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/selected-t16-three-role-cycle-seedc375/verify.py\npython3 -B research/selected-t16-three-role-cycle-seedc375/test_verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-t16-three-role-cycle-seedc375 --check-only\n```\n\nThe direct verifier and four controls passed under Python 3.14.7. The registered full replay asks for Python 3.12, which is not installed in this environment; the source-pinned package is ready for that replay in CI.\n\nThe current selected review and source manifest are pinned in `SOURCES.json`. This does not change the selected record. Prepared by Codex with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; the selected owner-map and construction lineage are credited in the README.",
